    "updated_at": "2026-11-15T12:18:07Z",
    "body": "Reproduced on Windows (local, debug, `cargo xtask gate test ... --exact`). The failure is not flaky and not specific to the runner.\n\nPanic text:\n\n```\nthread 'a_tapered_punch_is_refused_at_post_while_the_file_states_no_guide_heights' panicked at crates\\app\\tests\\sodick_alc400g.rs:145:60:\n5 deg is inside the 25 deg limit: \"Invalid(\\\"a 5.000 degree taper is asked, and machine Sodick ALC400G states no edm.lower_guide_z and edm.upper_guide_z - a tapered wire's guide positions are read from them; set the taper to 0\\\")\"\n```\n\nCause: PR #1818 (commit `ceafc0f8f`, the fix for #1800). It adds `wire_edm::taper_door` to `wire_gate`. Now `CreateOperation` refuses the tapered punch with the guide-height words. Before, the first refusal came at the post. The test expects the create step to pass, so the `expect` on line 145 fails.\n\nThe product still refuses the taper, and it refuses it earlier. No program is posted. The output is correct. Only the expectation of the test is stale. PR #1818 did not change `sodick_alc400g.rs`, and the test runs in a slow step, so its quick gate did not run it.\n\nPlan: change the test. It will pin the refusal at the command door. It will also keep the refusal at post: the op is made on a machine with guide heights, then the shipped file is mounted, and the post must refuse. I change the priority to P2, because the failure is only in the test.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
